---
description: Keep Vue props on the props object — do not destructure defineProps
globs: "**/*.vue"
alwaysApply: false
---

# Vue props: no destructuring

Always assign `defineProps` to `props` and read fields as `props.foo`. Do not destructure props — including Vue 3.5+ reactive destructure — so script usage stays consistent.

Keep `withDefaults(defineProps<...>(), { ... })` when the component already uses it.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — destructure defineProps (even Vue 3.5+ reactive destructure)
const { label } = defineProps<{ label: string }>()

// ❌ BAD — destructure the props object in script
const props = defineProps<{ label: string }>()
const { label } = props

// ✅ GOOD — typed props, access via props
const props = defineProps<{ label: string }>()
watch(() => props.label, () => {})

// ✅ GOOD — defaults
const props = withDefaults(defineProps<{ color?: 'green' | 'gray' }>(), {
  color: 'gray'
})

// ✅ GOOD — template-only (no script access)
defineProps<{ title: string }>()
```

In templates, `{{ label }}` is fine. In `<script setup>`, always use `props.label`.
